//! Kimi-K3 pre-tokenizer: differential test against the reference pattern.
//!
//! GENERATED by scripts/gen_k3_pretok_cases.py — do not edit by hand.
//!
//! Every expected split below was produced by running K3's ACTUAL `pat_str`
//! (from `tokenization_kimi.py`) through the `regex` module. They are not a
//! second reading of the pattern written out by hand, so this fails if the Rust
//! port misunderstands the pattern, not merely if it misimplements what I
//! believed the pattern to be.
//!
//! Regenerate after any change to the split, and diff the fixture.

use colibri_tokenizer::k3_pretokenize;

/// `(input, expected_pieces)` — see the module note on provenance.
